    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "b1",
        "chapter_id": "ch1",
        "text": "Liora Vale carried the brass gate key. Wren was Liora Vale's childhood nickname, used by all her friends. There was only one woman: Liora Vale and Wren were two names for the same person.",
        "source": {
          "href": "text/ch1.xhtml",
          "element_id": "b1",
          "tag": "p"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "b2",
        "chapter_id": "ch1",
        "text": "Liora left the town to survey the northern pass, taking her brass key with her. Her absence lasted seven years.",
        "source": {
          "href": "text/ch1.xhtml",
          "element_id": "b2",
          "tag": "p"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "b3",
        "chapter_id": "ch2",
        "text": "Wren returned to the old gate seven years later. She was Liora Vale, the very same woman who had left with the brass key, now older and wearing a traveling cloak. No substitute, relative, or namesake had taken her place.",
        "source": {
          "href": "text/ch2.xhtml",
          "element_id": "b3",
          "tag": "p"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "b4",
        "chapter_id": "ch2",
        "text": "She put the original brass key in the lock. The town register recorded her full name as Liora Vale and her familiar name as Wren.",
        "source": {
          "href": "text/ch2.xhtml",
          "element_id": "b4",
          "tag": "p"
        }
      }
    ],
